WEBVTT

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:02.980
The defendant, Namase Masato,

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:05.180
ignored article 1 of the
magic-prohibition law and,

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:08.480
despite being fully aware
of the risks involved,

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:12.230
used ice magic to instantly
freeze the victim,

00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:15.740
a fellow stuntman,
which then stopped his heart,

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:17.610
thus killing him.

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:18.810
...No...

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:20.240
...My manager...

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:23.620
Your manager, Mr. Ooizumi, stated that

00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:26.250
he only allowed you to use magic
since you threatened him.

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:30.090
Did you do it to feel the
thrill of using magic again?

00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:31.390
...No...

00:00:31.390 --> 00:00:32.590
In the end,

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:36.680
wizards can never be human.

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:39.840
The prosecution recommends that
the defendant be sentenced to death.

00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:53.320
Did you have that dream again?

00:00:53.570 --> 00:00:57.950
You know it was the judge
who made that decision.

00:01:04.450 --> 00:01:07.090
How about tonight,
...I lie down next to you...

00:01:07.090 --> 00:01:08.960
How about I cut some
bacon off your back?

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:10.830
I'm not lying!

00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:13.340
I was asked to do it!

00:01:13.340 --> 00:01:17.090
I don't know anything
about Grimoire 365!

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:25.970
I will carry my indomitable hope into the dark night

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:25.970
yami no naka no shinjitsu ga hikari kagayaku you ni

00:01:26.180 --> 00:01:32.270
so that it may light a shining fire of truth there

00:01:26.180 --> 00:01:32.270
kagi no nai kibou wo tokihanatou

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:47.750
I was born bleeding from my hands,

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:47.750
naze te no hira no kizu wo daite umareochita imi

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:51.710
and why was I born not a thousand years in the past or the future,

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:51.710
sennen kako demo mirai demo naku

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:53.040
but in the present?

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:53.040
erabareta ima

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:57.380
The scales of justice are fragile

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:57.380
zen'aku hakaru tenbin wa zeijaku

00:01:57.380 --> 00:02:02.430
The waning, waxing moon calls to a flower on the earth

00:01:57.380 --> 00:02:02.430
michikakeru tsuki ga izanau gisei no chi ni saita

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:04.350
the color of blood

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:04.350
chi no iro no hana

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:06.850
I will give all I have

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:06.850
tatta hitotsu kanau nara

00:02:06.850 --> 00:02:09.560
if it means one of my wishes will come true

00:02:06.850 --> 00:02:09.560
subete wo sasageyou

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:12.730
I have a "post nubila phoebus" kind of personality

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:12.730
post nubila phoebus kokoro

00:02:12.820 --> 00:02:14.690
which I will show the world

00:02:12.820 --> 00:02:14.690
kaze ni hanatte

00:02:14.570 --> 00:02:17.690
I want to slash apart the curtain of raven black,

00:02:14.570 --> 00:02:17.690
shikkoku no curtain hikichigiri

00:02:17.730 --> 00:02:20.340
and look at a new world

00:02:17.730 --> 00:02:20.340
chigau sora wo mitemitai

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:22.990
My love stabs at the cracks

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:22.990
sabita unmei no hibiware

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:25.470
of a stagnant fate

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:25.470
omoi wa nejikonde

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:28.370
No matter how long the storm lasts,

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:28.370
donnani arasoi tsuzuketemo

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:30.960
time itself will not stop breathing

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:30.960
toki wa kokyuu wo yamenai

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:33.750
What remains after destruction, rebirth,

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:33.750
kowashite tsunde kowashite

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:36.210
and further destruction?

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:36.210
nani ga nokoru darou

00:02:36.210 --> 00:02:38.920
I'm sure I can put an end to a thousand nights of doubt

00:02:36.210 --> 00:02:38.920
sou nanajuuokuban no mayoi mo

00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:42.090
and to the system of the world

00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:42.090
sono haichizu wa kakikaerareru

00:02:42.090 --> 00:02:44.760
I'm sure that one day I will find a place where I can shine

00:02:42.090 --> 00:02:44.760
moetsukitemo kagayakeru basho e

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:48.970
even if only ashes will remain

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:48.970
itsuka tadoritsukeru

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:55.820
Love and Hate

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:55.820
Case 3

00:02:55.820 --> 00:02:58.570
Today's lunch box contains
the best of the best.

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:01.330
Thanks for the food!

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:05.330
...What the—?!

00:03:06.230 --> 00:03:08.830
It's delicious <i>and artistic!</i>

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:14.430
You perverted frog!

00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:17.300
Are you Sudou Cecil, of Butterfly?

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:20.300
Oh, wow. You really are.

00:03:20.710 --> 00:03:23.610
I'm so happy to have run into you here.

00:03:23.610 --> 00:03:24.640
You eating lunch?

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:28.140
Wh-Who are you?

00:03:28.710 --> 00:03:30.230
Pardon our late introductions.

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:31.900
This is who we are.

00:03:32.620 --> 00:03:35.400
..."Law Offices of Shark Knight"...

00:03:35.770 --> 00:03:38.280
My name is Sameoka Kiba.

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:40.360
...And I'm Kujira Shibuki...

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:41.450
Pleased to meet ya.

00:03:41.450 --> 00:03:43.450
Hello.

00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:46.260
That case with No Face
gave me the chills!

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:51.400
I still can't believe that you just
brought the robbers in on your own.

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:53.670
Thank you.

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:57.390
We don't have any wizard barristers
like you in our office.

00:03:57.390 --> 00:03:59.340
We think you'd be a wonderful addition.

00:03:59.340 --> 00:04:02.140
Not to mention that we pay
way more than Butterfly does.

00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:06.140
I'm happy with my current paycheck.

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:08.850
You may not know this yet,

00:04:08.850 --> 00:04:12.230
but Butterfly isn't too popular in our field.

00:04:12.230 --> 00:04:14.730
Working there won't benefit
you in any way whatsoever.

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:20.660
I hope you'll consider joining us.

00:04:23.540 --> 00:04:25.280
See ya!

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:28.340
They're pretty shifty.

00:04:29.060 --> 00:04:30.170
Yeah.

00:04:30.170 --> 00:04:32.860
Wasn't that Prince Shark?

00:04:32.860 --> 00:04:34.210
What did he want?

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:36.710
Butterfly Law Offices

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:36.710
Shark Knight tried to recruit <i>you</i>?

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:38.780
How could they just ignore me?

00:04:38.780 --> 00:04:41.340
Haven't they <i>seen my body?</i>

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:43.510
Don't you think it's weird, though?

00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:46.850
At Shark Knight,
all the wizard barristers are men.

00:04:46.850 --> 00:04:49.560
I'd just thought that
they didn't hire women.

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:52.700
So they're incredibly hot,
and yet they're still looking for a girl?

00:04:52.700 --> 00:04:55.560
Why Cecilcchi, anyway?

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:58.220
Maybe it's because they
don't see her as a girl?

00:04:58.220 --> 00:04:59.930
That's so mean, Natcchi!

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:01.650
Don't call me that.

00:05:02.380 --> 00:05:06.030
If that had been me, I would've totally
gone with them with drool on my face.

00:05:08.110 --> 00:05:11.790
Oh, Hachiya, call for you
from Inspector Quinn.

00:05:13.540 --> 00:05:14.920
It's been a while.

00:05:15.380 --> 00:05:17.250
Do you remember me?

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:20.540
...<i>"Confidential..."</i>

00:05:20.540 --> 00:05:22.720
<i>"Saotome Mayu, age 25."</i>

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:24.120
<i>"Wave magic."</i>

00:05:24.120 --> 00:05:28.890
<i>"Her magic can vibrate air at high
...frequencies to a destructive effect."</i>

00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:33.220
<i>"One of these explosions
...has killed a person."</i>

00:05:33.220 --> 00:05:35.400
<i>"The body has yet to be identified."</i>

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:39.230
<i>"At this time, the suspect is
...keeping quiet about her motive."</i>

00:05:40.070 --> 00:05:41.450
Hey, we're indoors.

00:05:41.450 --> 00:05:43.480
Can't you read?

00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:48.020
I read in a magazine that I'd have
good luck today if I smoked at work.

00:05:48.020 --> 00:05:50.390
What the hell kind of magazine is that?

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:52.860
Is this about that explosion?

00:05:52.860 --> 00:05:54.880
Right. It's her statement.

00:05:55.420 --> 00:05:58.790
Wizard barrister: Butterfly's Hachiya?

00:05:58.790 --> 00:06:00.130
She requested him specifically.

00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:03.010
She said she wouldn't talk
unless we called him.

00:06:03.690 --> 00:06:05.300
Oh?

00:06:05.790 --> 00:06:10.100
I was shocked when I heard that
you're a wizard barrister now, Hachiya.

00:06:10.790 --> 00:06:13.100
Why did you cause that explosion?

00:06:13.510 --> 00:06:14.850
Just to let off some steam.

00:06:14.850 --> 00:06:18.850
I didn't think you were
the type to commit crimes.

00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:25.070
My life changed after
that incident two years ago.

00:06:25.610 --> 00:06:26.820
...The verdict...

00:06:26.820 --> 00:06:30.530
Defendant Namase Masato,
who is a stuntman,

00:06:30.530 --> 00:06:33.830
had brought up the idea of using
magic on stage to his manager.

00:06:33.830 --> 00:06:37.120
Despite knowing the dangers,
he still used his ice magic,

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:39.080
thereby causing the victim's death.

00:06:39.450 --> 00:06:41.420
Considering this was by your own decision,

00:06:41.420 --> 00:06:44.590
it is not manslaughter, but a murder.

00:06:45.250 --> 00:06:46.010
It wasn't me!

00:06:46.010 --> 00:06:49.380
The manager was the one
who suggested I use magic!

00:06:50.430 --> 00:06:51.930
It wasn't me!

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:53.680
Please believe me!

00:06:54.210 --> 00:06:55.180
Order!

00:06:56.110 --> 00:06:57.690
Our verdict is that

00:06:57.690 --> 00:07:00.360
you have violated article 1
of the magic-prohibition law,

00:07:00.360 --> 00:07:04.840
causing harm to others with magic,
and have committed murder.

00:07:04.840 --> 00:07:09.200
As requested,
you are sentenced to death.

00:07:11.490 --> 00:07:12.990
...I didn't do it...

00:07:12.990 --> 00:07:13.910
...I...

00:07:19.120 --> 00:07:21.210
The sealing cuffs!

00:07:23.210 --> 00:07:26.390
The magic-sealing system isn't activating?

00:07:36.550 --> 00:07:37.850
Masato!

00:07:37.850 --> 00:07:39.140
Masato!

00:07:41.900 --> 00:07:43.790
What's wrong, Masato?

00:07:43.790 --> 00:07:44.900
Masato!

00:07:54.150 --> 00:07:57.620
Masato!

00:08:00.370 --> 00:08:06.380
Masato died because you let your
prejudice against Wuds influence the trial.

00:08:06.890 --> 00:08:09.260
You never stopped to think that
he might've been a victim himself.

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:12.140
I'm joking.

00:08:12.140 --> 00:08:16.140
You were only doing
your job as a prosecutor.

00:08:16.850 --> 00:08:19.550
And? You doubt her motives?

00:08:20.440 --> 00:08:24.130
I'm not entirely certain,
but I believe there's another reason.

00:08:24.130 --> 00:08:25.290
And the sentence?

00:08:25.290 --> 00:08:26.360
I'm asking for life.

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:28.550
I'll avoid the death sentence at all costs.

00:08:28.550 --> 00:08:31.370
Do you have an assistant in mind?

00:08:31.370 --> 00:08:34.370
I'd like to take this case on my own.

00:08:36.690 --> 00:08:38.200
Come on, Hachimitsu!

00:08:38.200 --> 00:08:41.080
I can't believe that Hachimitsu
used to be a prosecutor.

00:08:41.080 --> 00:08:43.760
But according to article 6
of the magic-prohibition law,

00:08:43.760 --> 00:08:47.460
Wuds aren't allowed to work in public positions
involving legal administration, right?

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:49.920
Yeah, apart from wizard barristers.

00:08:49.920 --> 00:08:53.060
Hachimitsu's awakening
was two years ago.

00:08:53.060 --> 00:08:57.160
He was discharged as a prosecutor
and became a wizard barrister.

00:08:57.160 --> 00:09:00.080
That's rather rare.

00:09:00.080 --> 00:09:02.480
Most awaken during puberty.

00:09:02.480 --> 00:09:05.230
His awakening probably happened
after losing his virginity.

00:09:05.230 --> 00:09:07.320
Huh? Two years ago?

00:09:08.440 --> 00:09:12.150
Silly, don't take anything
Sasorin says seriously.

00:09:12.150 --> 00:09:16.810
Sheesh, I can't deal with
Sori's perverted jokes.

00:09:16.810 --> 00:09:19.550
Cecil, do you have a minute?

00:09:19.550 --> 00:09:20.750
Y-Yes.

00:09:20.750 --> 00:09:22.740
I wonder if Hachimitsu picked her.

00:09:22.740 --> 00:09:25.300
Cecilcchi is so popular.

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:26.000
Declaratory Judgment

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:26.000
Pet Ownership

00:09:27.390 --> 00:09:28.880
Natcchi!

00:09:28.880 --> 00:09:30.760
Wanna get some lunch?

00:09:30.760 --> 00:09:34.430
There's no way Buzz-Buzz Hachimitsu
would choose Cecilun.

00:09:34.430 --> 00:09:35.960
That's not the issue.

00:09:35.960 --> 00:09:39.010
Are you upset that Cecilun
is getting all the work?

00:09:40.830 --> 00:09:42.270
Honestly, yes.

00:09:42.270 --> 00:09:44.290
Cecil is younger than I am,

00:09:44.290 --> 00:09:46.270
and since we started at the same time,
I don't want to fall behind her.

00:09:46.890 --> 00:09:49.340
I'm sorry, I've said too much.

00:09:49.340 --> 00:09:51.930
Please don't tell Cecil what I just said.

00:09:51.930 --> 00:09:53.640
I won't.

00:09:53.640 --> 00:09:59.370
But as a proud cynic, you're losing out.

00:10:00.180 --> 00:10:05.290
I haven't been handed any police cases
because I'm still inexperienced.

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:07.270
As much as I hate to admit it,

00:10:07.270 --> 00:10:10.800
Cecil might have more to offer than I do.

00:10:10.800 --> 00:10:12.000
That's the spirit.

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:14.800
I'm sure you'll make a great
barrister one day, Natcchi.

00:10:15.540 --> 00:10:16.680
That goes without saying.

00:10:18.810 --> 00:10:21.060
What? Magic?

00:10:21.060 --> 00:10:27.400
Yeah. My manager said he'd double
my pay if I used magic on the show.

00:10:27.400 --> 00:10:29.080
Are you sure that's okay?

00:10:29.080 --> 00:10:30.910
That's illegal, you know.

00:10:30.910 --> 00:10:33.900
But he said he'd fire me if I didn't do it.

00:10:34.700 --> 00:10:36.030
...And, well...

00:10:36.910 --> 00:10:39.550
I'd like to save some money.

00:10:39.550 --> 00:10:41.540
I'll work harder than I am right now.

00:10:43.930 --> 00:10:44.700
...So, Mayu...

00:10:45.710 --> 00:10:47.120
Will you move in with me?

00:10:47.120 --> 00:10:48.760
...Masato...

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:56.170
...Macal...

00:11:00.200 --> 00:11:04.270
If we combine the remains
...of the upper and lower jaws...

00:11:04.270 --> 00:11:06.530
Come on. Give us a match.

00:11:09.770 --> 00:11:09.810
Match

00:11:09.810 --> 00:11:09.860
Match

00:11:09.860 --> 00:11:09.900
Match

00:11:09.900 --> 00:11:09.940
Match

00:11:09.940 --> 00:11:11.190
Match

00:11:11.280 --> 00:11:13.780
I didn't lie to you.

00:11:13.780 --> 00:11:18.110
How do you explain the
victim's autopsy, then?

00:11:19.920 --> 00:11:22.390
Before he exploded, he had
a number of broken bones.

00:11:22.390 --> 00:11:24.080
They're from a lynching.

00:11:24.890 --> 00:11:25.910
I have no idea.

00:11:28.170 --> 00:11:31.880
We heard that you were acquainted
with Ooizumi, the victim.

00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:34.540
We've done our research.

00:11:34.540 --> 00:11:38.260
This was a premeditated murder
to avenge your boyfriend, right?

00:11:42.260 --> 00:11:43.510
Damn it!

00:11:43.510 --> 00:11:45.510
That damned wizard!

00:11:47.020 --> 00:11:48.450
Butterfly?

00:11:48.450 --> 00:11:49.520
About to start your interview?

00:11:49.520 --> 00:11:50.650
Yes.

00:11:52.580 --> 00:11:54.570
You've heard something, haven't you?

00:11:55.430 --> 00:11:57.690
The victim in the explosion was Ooizumi,

00:11:57.690 --> 00:11:59.780
a witness in the trial two years ago.

00:12:00.460 --> 00:12:03.280
We believe that Mayu
planned this murder.

00:12:04.100 --> 00:12:08.290
Hachiya, don't allow yourself
any pity for that woman.

00:12:08.290 --> 00:12:11.090
Ms. Mayu and the victim
were acquaintances.

00:12:12.270 --> 00:12:16.690
The only thing you've accomplished
is making humans fear Wuds.

00:12:16.690 --> 00:12:18.670
Please tell us your motive.

00:12:19.130 --> 00:12:20.500
I already did.

00:12:20.500 --> 00:12:21.760
I was just letting off some steam.

00:12:22.300 --> 00:12:25.040
What was your relationship
with Mr. Ooizumi?

00:12:25.040 --> 00:12:28.020
I haven't seen Ooizumi
since Masato died.

00:12:28.420 --> 00:12:30.520
It was just a coincidence
that he was involved.

00:12:31.530 --> 00:12:33.770
What do you think, Hachimitsu?

00:12:34.300 --> 00:12:37.800
The prosecution is going to
push for premeditated murder.

00:12:37.800 --> 00:12:41.870
We're going to argue that it was a
coincidence, and aim for a life sentence.

00:12:43.410 --> 00:12:47.020
...I understand how Ms. Mayu feels...

00:12:48.360 --> 00:12:50.260
I'm sorry, Hachimitsu,

00:12:50.260 --> 00:12:53.610
but I don't really care
...if it's a prosecutor or a judge...

00:12:53.610 --> 00:12:56.920
I hate people who are
prejudiced against Wuds.

00:12:56.920 --> 00:12:58.070
You "hate"?

00:12:58.070 --> 00:13:00.200
That doesn't sound like you, Sudou.

00:13:00.200 --> 00:13:04.690
There are numerous cases where defendants'
rights aren't upheld due to prejudice.

00:13:04.690 --> 00:13:07.620
Nobody bothers to lend them an ear.

00:13:08.390 --> 00:13:10.680
Humans and Wuds
cannot live together.

00:13:10.680 --> 00:13:13.600
That's what most humans believe.

00:13:13.600 --> 00:13:15.510
Do you agree?

00:13:15.510 --> 00:13:16.510
...I...

00:13:17.280 --> 00:13:19.150
still don't know.

00:13:20.170 --> 00:13:21.780
After becoming a Wud,

00:13:21.780 --> 00:13:24.160
many things have perplexed me.

00:13:24.160 --> 00:13:27.220
What had I been until then?

00:13:27.220 --> 00:13:32.290
That's why I want to find that answer by doing
everything I can—by being a wizard barrister.

00:13:33.710 --> 00:13:35.620
I <i>did drive Masato into a corner.</i>

00:13:35.620 --> 00:13:37.670
And Mayu <i>did commit a crime.</i>

00:13:37.670 --> 00:13:39.670
These are the undeniable facts.

00:13:40.230 --> 00:13:41.810
As a barrister,

00:13:41.810 --> 00:13:43.930
I will bear responsibility for this case.

00:13:47.530 --> 00:13:50.340
Regardless of whether it was
a premeditated murder or not,

00:13:50.340 --> 00:13:52.710
something feels terribly off here.

00:13:52.710 --> 00:13:57.110
It doesn't seem like she's staying mum just so
she gets off with a lighter sentence, either.

00:13:58.290 --> 00:13:59.610
Peach pie!

00:13:59.610 --> 00:14:03.240
Maybe she's trying to make you two
lose by not saying anything.

00:14:03.240 --> 00:14:05.220
What? That'd suck!

00:14:05.220 --> 00:14:07.450
If we lose too much,
the office will go bankrupt.

00:14:07.450 --> 00:14:09.620
Wait, bankrupt?

00:14:14.680 --> 00:14:16.500
...That haven will be...

00:14:16.500 --> 00:14:18.640
Too shocking!

00:14:18.640 --> 00:14:20.170
...H-Hey...

00:14:20.170 --> 00:14:22.510
<i>I'm the one in shock,
you perverted frog!</i>

00:14:29.790 --> 00:14:32.020
Thank you for working with me.

00:14:32.020 --> 00:14:33.520
Thank you, as well.

00:14:37.370 --> 00:14:38.520
Hachiya.

00:14:46.400 --> 00:14:47.860
...Um...

00:14:47.860 --> 00:14:48.790
...What did she...

00:14:48.790 --> 00:14:52.220
Sudou, whatever happens,
don't interfere.

00:14:52.220 --> 00:14:52.870
Huh?

00:14:54.590 --> 00:14:57.120
The Court for Magic is now in session.

00:14:57.780 --> 00:15:02.500
The explosion that occurred was
a premeditated attempt to murder

00:15:02.500 --> 00:15:05.880
the former manager of Magical Hero
Production, Mr. Ooizumi, was it not?

00:15:06.270 --> 00:15:07.190
No.

00:15:07.190 --> 00:15:09.390
I only wanted to display my magic.

00:15:09.770 --> 00:15:12.890
So you hadn't seen
Mr. Ooizumi in two years?

00:15:12.890 --> 00:15:13.800
No.

00:15:13.800 --> 00:15:15.890
I didn't even want to see his face.

00:15:15.890 --> 00:15:18.900
I'm sure you didn't want
to remember that case.

00:15:18.900 --> 00:15:22.980
Neither the police nor the
judges tried to help you.

00:15:22.980 --> 00:15:25.490
Your Honor, this is irrelevant.

00:15:25.490 --> 00:15:29.730
Would the defense please ask questions
to back up the defendant's statement?

00:15:29.730 --> 00:15:32.490
And why are you dressed like that again?

00:15:32.490 --> 00:15:34.980
I believe I've already told you that

00:15:34.980 --> 00:15:37.000
these are my battle clothes!

00:15:37.000 --> 00:15:39.720
Will the defense feign ignorance?

00:15:39.720 --> 00:15:42.250
That'd be the smart thing to do.

00:15:43.630 --> 00:15:46.780
The prosecution requests
the death penalty.

00:15:46.780 --> 00:15:51.640
The defendant's motive was to get revenge
on her boyfriend's former manager,

00:15:51.640 --> 00:15:54.460
Mr. Ooizumi, who had
testified unfavorably at his trial.

00:15:54.460 --> 00:15:56.140
Therefore, this was premeditated murder.

00:15:56.140 --> 00:16:00.980
There is no evidence linking
this case to the one two years ago.

00:16:00.980 --> 00:16:04.660
Therefore, I think we should
believe the defendant's affidavit.

00:16:04.660 --> 00:16:09.650
Underlying factors include resentment regarding
discrimination and prejudice against wizards.

00:16:10.080 --> 00:16:14.120
Given these extenuating circumstances,
we request a life sentence.

00:16:16.270 --> 00:16:17.410
...The verdict...

00:16:17.800 --> 00:16:20.400
We sentence the defendant
to life imprisonment.

00:16:20.400 --> 00:16:22.370
As the defense stated,

00:16:22.370 --> 00:16:25.740
there is no solid proof that
this was a premeditated murder.

00:16:25.740 --> 00:16:29.910
Based on the reasonable doubt standard,

00:16:29.910 --> 00:16:33.930
we reject the claim that this case is
connected to the case from two years ago.

00:16:34.720 --> 00:16:35.930
...Life...

00:16:36.880 --> 00:16:38.120
imprisonment?

00:16:39.200 --> 00:16:42.440
So Masato, who killed someone
accidentally, gets the death penalty,

00:16:42.440 --> 00:16:45.070
while I, with murderous
intent, get life in prison?

00:16:46.390 --> 00:16:47.940
You make me laugh.

00:16:47.940 --> 00:16:50.700
You're all incompetent,
you know that?

00:16:50.700 --> 00:16:55.530
There's no way I'd forget
that trial from two years ago!

00:16:56.520 --> 00:16:58.660
When I finally found him,

00:16:59.290 --> 00:17:00.820
my heart was set aflutter.

00:17:05.660 --> 00:17:07.450
When I roughed him up a little,

00:17:07.450 --> 00:17:11.340
he quickly confessed to the fact
that the witnesses all arranged

00:17:11.340 --> 00:17:13.010
their testimony to frame Masato.

00:17:20.890 --> 00:17:22.690
As promised, I removed them.

00:17:22.690 --> 00:17:24.980
Now you're free to
take your revenge on me.

00:17:24.980 --> 00:17:26.480
I'm prepared.

00:17:26.480 --> 00:17:29.570
You can torment or kill me
to your heart's content.

00:17:29.980 --> 00:17:32.960
You really <i>have repented, huh?</i>

00:17:32.960 --> 00:17:34.570
But it's too late!

00:17:34.570 --> 00:17:36.920
I've already decided to kill
everyone involved in that trial

00:17:36.920 --> 00:17:41.080
right here in the courtroom
where Masato died!

00:17:47.460 --> 00:17:48.420
Not again!

00:17:51.170 --> 00:17:52.050
Look out!

00:17:55.680 --> 00:17:56.640
Stop it!

00:17:56.640 --> 00:17:58.430
Killing me should be enough!

00:17:58.430 --> 00:18:00.060
All of you are guilty!

00:18:00.060 --> 00:18:03.060
The Court for Magic
should just disappear!

00:18:10.650 --> 00:18:13.510
And I'll take care of you
...with my own two hands...

00:18:17.480 --> 00:18:18.660
Hachimitsu!

00:18:20.200 --> 00:18:21.600
Your Honor!

00:18:21.600 --> 00:18:24.620
I wish to apply article 10
of the magic-prohibition law!

00:18:24.980 --> 00:18:26.290
Permission granted!

00:18:29.590 --> 00:18:31.500
<i>Cecil Diaboloid!</i>

00:18:31.500 --> 00:18:32.760
Stop!

00:18:33.510 --> 00:18:34.990
...Don't worry about me...

00:18:35.740 --> 00:18:36.760
Just save everyone else.

00:18:39.720 --> 00:18:41.580
...Please, stop it, Ms. Mayu...

00:18:41.580 --> 00:18:45.270
Please don't hurt your heart any further!

00:18:46.030 --> 00:18:49.530
I have a family member
who was sentenced to death too.

00:18:49.530 --> 00:18:53.700
The Court for Magic should be
for Wuds, but no one helped her!

00:18:55.280 --> 00:18:56.950
...But...

00:18:56.950 --> 00:18:59.030
You know, don't you?

00:18:59.030 --> 00:19:02.660
That doing this won't change a thing!

00:19:02.660 --> 00:19:03.660
...Shut up...

00:19:03.660 --> 00:19:04.910
Shut up!

00:19:08.120 --> 00:19:08.920
Sudou!

00:19:12.380 --> 00:19:14.960
This is nothing compared
to Masato's suffering.

00:19:19.700 --> 00:19:20.680
Ms. Mayu!

00:19:21.150 --> 00:19:23.390
If the law won't help,

00:19:23.390 --> 00:19:25.430
then I'll have to take things
into my own hands!

00:19:27.190 --> 00:19:32.190
No!

00:19:44.920 --> 00:19:46.000
...You little—!

00:19:46.000 --> 00:19:48.660
I still haven't gotten to the truth!

00:19:48.660 --> 00:19:50.630
Masato's death was planned!

00:19:50.630 --> 00:19:51.750
Huh?

00:20:12.020 --> 00:20:13.670
Why did you shoot her?!

00:20:13.670 --> 00:20:14.990
Why?!

00:20:20.700 --> 00:20:22.160
Do you really need to ask?

00:20:22.690 --> 00:20:24.260
I'm a cop.

00:20:26.000 --> 00:20:27.160
...But...

00:20:30.740 --> 00:20:31.720
It's fine.

00:20:32.400 --> 00:20:33.670
Just let me die.

00:20:34.920 --> 00:20:35.980
...No...

00:20:37.060 --> 00:20:39.180
...Labone and Macal...

00:20:39.180 --> 00:20:42.680
...Grimoire 365...

00:20:42.680 --> 00:20:43.330
...What—

00:20:48.490 --> 00:20:50.690
You can't die!

00:20:52.770 --> 00:20:54.910
You have to live!

00:21:01.990 --> 00:21:06.490
So Hachimitsu is under
house arrest for a week?

00:21:06.490 --> 00:21:08.890
Removing the sealing cuffs

00:21:08.890 --> 00:21:13.710
generally means suspension or
losing his wizard barrister's license.

00:21:13.710 --> 00:21:16.210
How much did getting
him off lightly cost you?

00:21:17.180 --> 00:21:19.210
It's a secret.

00:21:19.210 --> 00:21:22.220
I heard you awakened
to a new magic, Cecilun.

00:21:22.220 --> 00:21:26.730
I thought I only had the
...power to make Diaboloids...

00:21:27.740 --> 00:21:30.620
Oh, be sure to register
that with the government.

00:21:30.620 --> 00:21:33.730
We don't want to be fined under article 5
of the magic-prohibition law again, do we?

00:21:34.980 --> 00:21:38.940
And here I thought Hachiya
wasn't the type to do anything rash.

00:21:45.630 --> 00:21:49.750
A skilled Wud of Labone
may become a threat to Macal.

00:21:49.750 --> 00:21:52.000
Just like Masato and Mayu.

00:21:53.180 --> 00:21:58.000
But who could've expected
Sudou Cecil's magic to awaken further?

00:21:58.780 --> 00:22:01.760
If the prophecies in
Grimoire 365 are true,

00:22:01.760 --> 00:22:05.010
nothing could be more fortunate for us.

00:22:06.390 --> 00:22:09.200
I'll be relying on you even more.

00:22:25.700 --> 00:22:32.660
My heart may cry silently,

00:22:25.700 --> 00:22:32.660
kokoro ga donna ni namida afuretemo

00:22:33.040 --> 00:22:40.220
but I still want to behold the blue sky

00:22:33.040 --> 00:22:40.220
hitomi ni aozora utsushiteitai

00:22:40.470 --> 00:22:47.780
I want to have something like the strength of flowers

00:22:40.470 --> 00:22:47.780
concrete-iro no machi no katasumi ni

00:22:47.780 --> 00:22:55.220
which bloom in the nooks of the endless concrete of the city

00:22:47.780 --> 00:22:55.220
sotto saku hana no tsuyosa wo manetai

00:22:55.220 --> 00:23:02.620
Starting today, I won't try to wriggle out by saying

00:22:55.220 --> 00:23:02.620
maegami ga jama de mienai nante iiwake

00:23:02.620 --> 00:23:06.450
that I saw nothing because my hair was in the way

00:23:02.620 --> 00:23:06.450
kyou kara shinai

00:23:07.410 --> 00:23:14.870
Beyond the horizon, my future awaits me,

00:23:07.410 --> 00:23:14.870
chiheisen no mukou ni ashita ga matteru kara

00:23:14.870 --> 00:23:20.130
so I will let the sun in my heart

00:23:14.870 --> 00:23:20.130
kono mune no hitotsu no taiyou

00:23:20.130 --> 00:23:22.170
shine out far and wide

00:23:20.130 --> 00:23:22.170
tooku hanatte

00:23:22.170 --> 00:23:29.510
I will overtake the earth's rotation on the path I walk,

00:23:22.170 --> 00:23:29.510
chikyuu no jiten wo oikosu kurai hitamuki ni arukou

00:23:29.510 --> 00:23:37.600
with trusting love inside my heart

00:23:29.510 --> 00:23:37.600
shinjiru omoi dakishimete doko made mo
